# Compiled binaries
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/bin/
/dist/

# Binaries accidentally built in the repo root (e.g. `go build ./cmd/vpn-ca`,
# `make ca-init`). Prefer building into /bin/; these anchors keep a stray one
# out of a commit. .exe variants are covered by *.exe above.
/vpn-bot
/vpn-ca
/vpn-client
/vpn-ctl
/vpn-gui
/vpn-helper
/vpn-server

# Same, but next to their package — `go build ./cmd/vpn-gui` from inside the
# command directory drops the binary there, where the root anchors miss it.
/cmd/*/vpn-bot
/cmd/*/vpn-ca
/cmd/*/vpn-client
/cmd/*/vpn-ctl
/cmd/*/vpn-gui
/cmd/*/vpn-helper
/cmd/*/vpn-server

# Generated CA material — NEVER commit secrets
/ca-data/
*.key
*.pem
*.vpnio
# CA backups (vpn-ca backup). Encrypted, but a committed one turns the whole
# security of the CA into "how good is that passphrase" — and it would stay in
# the history after any later removal.
*.vpnio-ca
# Passphrase files handed to `vpn-ca backup -passphrase-file`
*.passphrase

# Local planning notes — not part of the published project
/ROADMAP.md
/TECH_ROADMAP.md
/BUSINESS_PLAN.md

# Claude Code runtime/local files (lock files, per-user local settings)
.claude/*.lock
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated UI mockup screenshots (regenerate from docs/ui/mockup.html)
docs/ui/shot-*.png

# IDE / editor
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
